# An ability a resolved effect grants is part of that effect, whose text was fixed as it was created (CR 611.2c): a text
# change on the permanent afterwards changes its own text (CR 612.1), not the effects on it (Artificial Evolution's ruling:
# "It will not change any effects that are on the permanent"). Den of the Bugbear's activation resolves: until end of turn it
# is a 3/2 red Goblin with "Whenever this creature attacks, create a 1/1 red Goblin creature token that's tapped and
# attacking." Then Artificial Evolution replaces Goblin with Elf in the Den's text. The Den stays a Goblin (the effect set
# that type), and its granted trigger still makes a Goblin when it attacks: Bot2 takes 3 + 1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Den of the Bugbear
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Artificial Evolution
Island
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

